OL,3,GNEWSAMelon and aubergine success in hot
OL,4,Asummer experiment
OL,5,
OL,6,FWatermelons and aubergines are not
OL,7,Fcrops you might traditionally spot
OL,8,Fbeing grown in the UK, but an
OL,9,Fexperiment this summer found them to be
OL,10,Fperforming well in the unusually
OL,11,Fpersistent warm weather.
OL,13,FThe exotic fruits were successfully
OL,14,Fgrown at Asthall Manor, near Burford,
OL,15,FOxfordshire, as part of a scheme to
OL,16,Fboost food resilience in the face of
OL,17,Fclimate change.
OL,19,FThe seed experiment coincided with the
OL,20,FUK's hottest summer on record - making
OL,21,Fconditions more appropriate for growing
OL,22,Fthe tropical crops.
OL,23,APub: 13-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB S Eng NewsC  Reg TVF Weather
